abstract: "In Lean 4 with Mathlib we formalize two facts about the binary Goldbach conjecture. First, the headline endpoints of the goldbach-lean development (Chen 1+2, Li-Liu 1+1.9, Wu 1+1.8938) are logical consequences of binary Goldbach: set the second multiplier to 1. Second, Theorem 1.1 of arXiv:2611.09007v1, read under the paper's own definition of big-O (a limit ratio equal to a nonzero constant), already implies binary Goldbach; its proof lists the current case G(2n) among the assumptions, which is circular, and it separately takes positivity of G(2n-2) as an input that already presupposes the required positivity under the literal reading and lacks a basis under the standard reading. Eight theorems are kernel-checked with axioms contained in {propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound}. This does not prove the Goldbach conjecture, and no claim of priority is made beyond the timestamped record."
